NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Templates are reusable starting points for projects. They include source files and metadata, and can also declare add-on dependencies."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"use-a-template","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use a Template"}]},{"type":"code","value":"tanstack create my-app --template ecommerce\ntanstack create my-app --template https://example.com/template.json\ntanstack create my-app --template ./template.json","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--template"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts both URL/path values and built-in template IDs."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"create-a-template","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create a Template"}]},{"type":"code","value":"# 1. Create a project with the shape you want\ntanstack create my-template --add-ons clerk,drizzle,sentry\n\n# 2. Initialize template metadata\ncd my-template\ntanstack template init\n\n# 3. Edit template-info.json, then compile the output JSON\ntanstack template compile\n\n# 4. Use or distribute the compiled template file\ntanstack create new-app --template ./template.json","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"maintain-a-template","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maintain a Template"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the source project changes:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"cd my-template\ntanstack template compile","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Then publish the updated "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"template.json"},{"type":"text","value":" to the URL your team uses."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"registry-format","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Registry Format"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Registry entries can expose templates under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"templates"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"starters"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"use-a-template","text":"Use a Template","level":2},{"id":"create-a-template","text":"Create a Template","level":2},{"id":"maintain-a-template","text":"Maintain a Template","level":2},{"id":"registry-format","text":"Registry Format","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTemplates are reusable starting points for projects. They include source files and metadata, and can also declare add-on dependencies.\n\n## Use a Template\n\n```bash\ntanstack create my-app --template ecommerce\ntanstack create my-app --template https://example.com/template.json\ntanstack create my-app --template ./template.json\n```\n\n`--template` accepts both URL/path values and built-in template IDs.\n\n## Create a Template\n\n```bash\n# 1. Create a project with the shape you want\ntanstack create my-template --add-ons clerk,drizzle,sentry\n\n# 2. Initialize template metadata\ncd my-template\ntanstack template init\n\n# 3. Edit template-info.json, then compile the output JSON\ntanstack template compile\n\n# 4. Use or distribute the compiled template file\ntanstack create new-app --template ./template.json\n```\n\n## Maintain a Template\n\nWhen the source project changes:\n\n```bash\ncd my-template\ntanstack template compile\n```\n\nThen publish the updated `template.json` to the URL your team uses.\n\n## Registry Format\n\nRegistry entries can expose templates under `templates` or `starters`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: templates\ntitle: Templates\n---\n\nTemplates are reusable starting points for projects. They include source files and metadata, and can also declare add-on dependencies.\n\n## Use a Template\n\n```bash\ntanstack create my-app --template ecommerce\ntanstack create my-app --template https://example.com/template.json\ntanstack create my-app --template ./template.json\n```\n\n`--template` accepts both URL/path values and built-in template IDs.\n\n## Create a Template\n\n```bash\n# 1. Create a project with the shape you want\ntanstack create my-template --add-ons clerk,drizzle,sentry\n\n# 2. Initialize template metadata\ncd my-template\ntanstack template init\n\n# 3. Edit template-info.json, then compile the output JSON\ntanstack template compile\n\n# 4. Use or distribute the compiled template file\ntanstack create new-app --template ./template.json\n```\n\n## Maintain a Template\n\nWhen the source project changes:\n\n```bash\ncd my-template\ntanstack template compile\n```\n\nThen publish the updated `template.json` to the URL your team uses.\n\n## Registry Format\n\nRegistry entries can expose templates under `templates` or `starters`.\n"}
